{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n- **Snapshot comes from the contents and their fingerprint.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` checks `read_snapshot` for an empty string and a large Unicode string. It asserts that `content.format()` equals the original and that `fingerprint` equals the expected fingerprint. It also asserts that the recorded `Dependency::Node` carries the same fingerprint.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint` and `fingerprint.value == \"before\"`.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks the fingerprints of retained node contents against the expected `Fingerprint` values.\n- **No other read.**\n  - In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]`, the recorded reads are exactly `[1, 1, 1, 2]`. That is one read per node read, including `read_snapshot`.\n  - The `[1]` read-count assertion in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` shows the snapshot was built from the supplied contents. After the domain changed to \"after\", the snapshot's fingerprint and `format()` stayed at \"before\".\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` (same test file as the snapshot-versions test) asserts reads `[1,3,2,3,1]` with matching per-read fingerprints.\n  - The agent tests `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` and `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` (both in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`) assert the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprints for tool reads.\n- **Struct shape and constructor.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` is an integration test, so it only sees the public API. It builds a snapshot with `Snapshot::new`, which is the only construction path available outside the crate under `#[non_exhaustive]`. It asserts the public `content` and `fingerprint` fields. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory.\n- **`Clone` and `Debug` impls.** I found no test that exercises them. They are `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` on `Snapshot` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]`. A derive has no conditional and no transformation of its own, so the untested-obligation exemption applies.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "6783b2a4d0b4e2c98352e3255d1bb07342bc13f8749e2cee76ad5948eb461b69",
